{Spanish Opening (Ruy Lopez) for White: the Closed main line, the Marshall Attack and the Berlin Defence.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 {The Spanish bishop pressures the knight that defends e5.}
3... a6 (3... Nf6 {Berlin Defence.} 4. O-O Nxe4 5. d4 Nd6 6. Bxc6 dxc6 7. dxe5 Nf5
8. Qxd8+ Kxd8 {The Berlin endgame: White has the healthier pawn majority.})
4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 (7... O-O 8. c3 d5 {Marshall Attack.}
9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11. Rxe5 c6 12. d4 {White returns material later if needed, but keeps the extra pawn for now.})
8. c3 O-O 9. h3 {Stops ...Bg4 and prepares d4.} 9... Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Qc7 12. Nbd2 {Chigorin Variation: the knight heads for f1 and g3.} *
